\frametitle{Composer Data Bundle}
An operator planning a deployment can therefore read the per-module
capability directly rather than compose it in a browser, and the numbers
are the measured ones rather than the design-level ceiling: on the full
1,475-item corpus the invariants checker reaches 83.3\% alone and no
other module exceeds 10\%. Any composition estimate built on top of that
bundle should carry the caveat the ablation establishes --- the modules
are not independent, and the series-composition rule over-predicts the
union rate.
